WEBVTT

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:05.690
In a certain theater in a certain city,

00:00:05.690 --> 00:00:08.360
there was a girl.

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:13.530
Her dream was to become
the best singer in town.

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:17.570
And to have as many people
hear her song as possible.

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:22.410
I want to be your ideal heroine.

00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:25.420
That's impossible.

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:29.630
My song can't reach anyone.

00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:32.380
You understand that, don't you?

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:35.050
Because you're me.

00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:44.180
You look adorable, Ayumu!

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:47.560
You look gorgeous, Karin-san!

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:48.520
Yay!

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:50.770
You're the best, Ai-chan!

00:00:50.770 --> 00:00:53.530
You're all doing amazing!

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:57.570
Yes, hello! It's Kasumin's turn next!

00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:05.290
Next, please tell me what kind of school idol
you strive to be, Osaka-san.

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:10.630
I'd like to play a school idol
that's loved by all.

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:13.170
Could you clarify that a bit?

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:18.680
I try to imagine everyone's
ideal school idol and then become her.

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:25.600
Does that mean that you're playing the role
of a school idol loved by all as we speak?

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:26.810
Yes.

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:28.480
Oh, I see.

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:33.070
That sounds rather fitting
since you're in the Drama Club.

00:01:34.490 --> 00:01:40.030
By the way, I heard our Drama Club is doing
a joint drama festival with Touou Academy.

00:01:40.030 --> 00:01:46.870
Yes. Touou Academy and Nijigasaki
will each be doing their own programs.

00:01:46.870 --> 00:01:51.590
I heard that you were chosen for the
lead role of the Nijigasaki performance.

00:01:51.590 --> 00:01:56.760
Could we get a comment for all of
the loyal readers of the school paper?

00:01:56.760 --> 00:02:01.180
I'm going to do my best in this role,
so please come see the show.

00:02:04.430 --> 00:02:06.980
I-I'm being replaced?

00:02:06.980 --> 00:02:11.520
This role just wasn't for you, Shizuku.

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:13.520
If there's something I can work on,
please tell me!

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:16.110
I promise to do my best!

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:20.950
I wanted someone who could completely
put themselves out there for this role.

00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:23.120
Put myself out there?

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:25.830
The role is a singer,

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:31.380
so I thought you'd be perfect
since you're a school idol.

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:34.500
Please give me another chance!

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:42.300
<i>Let's go to the future!</i>
<i>Rainbow melodies</i>

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:55.070
<i>The rain clears up and reveals blue skies</i>

00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:58.070
<i>The winds of hope blow (Blowing)</i>

00:02:58.070 --> 00:03:02.990
<i>We can feel something coming</i>
<i>and we take our very first step</i>

00:03:02.990 --> 00:03:05.740
<i>The world is sparkling</i>

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:08.750
<i>And our hearts start to
well up with (Feelings)</i>

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:13.130
<i>"We want to start running right now!!"</i>
<i>(Move on! Move on!)</i>

00:03:13.130 --> 00:03:18.630
<i>The tiny melodies blend together (Our Colors)</i>

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:20.840
<i>Let's paint this arch, now</i>

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:24.430
<i>It resonates throughout the city</i>
<i>(Reaching for far blue sky!)</i>

00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:26.600
<i>Let's sing together!</i>

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:32.390
<i>My feelings are overflowing,</i>
<i>there's no stopping them now</i>

00:03:32.390 --> 00:03:35.060
<i>Rainbow-colored passions!!</i>

00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:37.270
<i>Colors painted in courage</i>

00:03:37.270 --> 00:03:39.940
<i>Let's create a bridge to the future</i>

00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:43.410
<i>Beyond the endless sky</i>

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:45.740
<i>Resounding sympathy</i>

00:03:45.740 --> 00:03:48.120
<i>Miracles are blooming</i>

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:51.330
<i>--Let's go! Shine towards
the future, melodies</i>

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:53.750
<i>--Yes, I know I'm not alone</i>
<i>--Let's go! Shine towards the future, melodies</i>

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:56.420
<i>You're all always by my side</i>

00:03:56.420 --> 00:04:02.470
<i>So let's connect our dreams together</i>

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:08.970
I want to sing.

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:11.890
I want everyone to hear my song.

00:04:11.890 --> 00:04:16.980
The emotions I put in my song are
happiness, heart, and a bit of passion.

00:04:20.690 --> 00:04:22.490
Shizuko?

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:24.740
Ta-da!

00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:29.410
Your first interview is now
in the school paper!

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:30.410
Wow!

00:04:30.410 --> 00:04:33.210
We all look awesome!

00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:35.670
Apparently, we're pretty popular.

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:38.420
Hopefully, they'll interview us again.

00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:43.550
Why don't we have them cover
one of our practices next time?

00:04:43.550 --> 00:04:46.930
That's a great idea, Setsuna-san!

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:50.220
Oh, good. Everything's the same as usual.

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:53.350
Hey, they talk about the upcoming
Drama Club performance, too.

00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:54.600
Ooh, let me see!

00:04:57.690 --> 00:05:01.030
It's so amazing you're playing the lead role!

00:05:01.030 --> 00:05:04.530
I'm definitely going to go see it.

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:07.660
Right. Thank you very much.

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:13.580
There's something wrong with Shizuku-chan?

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:20.380
Yeah. She seems gloomier than usual.

00:05:21.460 --> 00:05:25.880
I guess she might've seemed
that way... Or maybe not.

00:05:25.880 --> 00:05:30.640
Come to think of it, I heard
she got replaced as the lead role.

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:32.560
Wait, what?!

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:34.930
Someone from the Drama Club mentioned that.

00:05:34.930 --> 00:05:38.770
There's apparently going to be
another audition.

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:54.450
My song won't reach anyone.

00:05:54.450 --> 00:05:57.580
Do you remember when we were little?

00:05:58.710 --> 00:06:01.250
We were different from the others.

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:06.260
It may seem trivial, but
I was always anxious.

00:06:07.630 --> 00:06:10.470
What would I do if someone
thought I was weird?

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:13.100
If they disliked me?

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:15.850
I was always so scared.

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:21.690
That's why I started hiding my true self.

00:06:21.690 --> 00:06:25.190
And then... I felt so much better.

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:30.910
Ever since that day, I've been living a lie.

00:06:30.910 --> 00:06:36.580
There's no way that a song by someone
lying to herself is going to reach anyone.

00:06:38.660 --> 00:06:40.170
You know I'm right.

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:50.720
Shizuko captured!

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:52.390
K-Kasumi-san?

00:06:52.390 --> 00:06:54.180
--What is it?
--Rinako.

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:55.680
Roger.

00:06:55.680 --> 00:06:58.100
Rina-chan Board equipped.

00:06:58.100 --> 00:07:00.890
H-Hey, I can't see...

00:07:00.890 --> 00:07:03.400
All right, off we go!

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:05.110
Woo.

00:07:05.110 --> 00:07:08.070
Wh-What?!

00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:14.490
So this is... the legendary...

00:07:14.490 --> 00:07:16.620
Are we really eating this?

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:20.620
As a 0-5 contender against
the Mountain Pancake,

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:24.340
I shall share the secrets
in beating this monster.

00:07:24.340 --> 00:07:26.460
But you never beat it.

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:31.550
You just have to keep eating. Now, charge!

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:33.180
Thanks for the food.

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:37.720
It's so good!

00:07:37.720 --> 00:07:39.730
It's just too fluffy.

00:07:42.690 --> 00:07:45.020
Here, have some, Shizuko!

00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:51.070
It's good.

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:52.240
Right?

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:53.530
Happy.

00:07:53.530 --> 00:07:56.870
Let's go! We're gonna devour the whole thing!

00:08:01.160 --> 00:08:04.920
Rina-chan Board, I'm about to burst.

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:07.540
My first victory... Yay!

00:08:07.540 --> 00:08:08.670
We did it.

00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:09.760
Yay.

00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:12.880
So cute.

00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:16.640
Ooh, this is...

00:08:16.640 --> 00:08:20.470
She looks just like my Ophelia.

00:08:20.470 --> 00:08:21.930
I'm taking it.

00:08:21.930 --> 00:08:23.020
Okay.

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:31.650
What should I have?
Cute little Kasumin just doesn't know!

00:08:39.030 --> 00:08:41.950
Do you like old movies?

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:49.290
Did you start acting because
you watched movies like this?

00:08:50.170 --> 00:08:54.880
Maybe... That's part of it.

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:59.720
I feel like I'm the most
outgoing when I'm acting.

00:08:59.720 --> 00:09:02.060
I end up not caring how others feel about me.

00:09:03.850 --> 00:09:08.560
And I can forget the fact that
I'm Shizuku Osaka.

00:09:11.030 --> 00:09:13.820
Do you not like yourself?

00:09:14.780 --> 00:09:17.660
S-Sorry. I'm sure this sounds weird.

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:18.620
Just forget it.

00:09:18.620 --> 00:09:21.950
Hey! You look all gloomy again.

00:09:21.950 --> 00:09:25.250
You need to smile, Shizuko! Te-he!

00:09:25.250 --> 00:09:27.000
K-Kasumi-san.

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:30.880
Let's forget all the bad things today
and have a blast!

00:09:30.880 --> 00:09:35.670
Once you cheer up, you can audition again
for the lead role and win it back!

00:09:37.630 --> 00:09:40.350
So you knew...

00:09:40.350 --> 00:09:41.850
Yeah.

00:09:41.850 --> 00:09:45.310
It's not like you need to keep it a secret.

00:09:45.310 --> 00:09:48.060
We're rooting for you.

00:09:48.060 --> 00:09:52.480
And the least we can do
if you're depressed is listen...

00:09:52.480 --> 00:09:54.570
I'm fine!

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:58.240
Don't worry. I'm fine.

00:09:58.240 --> 00:10:00.660
Thank you both!

00:10:00.660 --> 00:10:02.990
Shizuku-chan...

00:10:02.990 --> 00:10:06.330
I should head home now. See you later!

00:10:19.470 --> 00:10:24.260
So you are scared... to
reveal your true self.

00:10:24.260 --> 00:10:25.850
Well...

00:10:25.850 --> 00:10:27.480
You don't want them to hate you?

00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:29.440
That's it, isn't it?

00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:32.360
I want to sing.

00:10:32.360 --> 00:10:34.730
I want to sing a song that'll
reach everyone's hearts.

00:10:36.190 --> 00:10:39.910
And to do that, you need to
put yourself out there.

00:10:42.160 --> 00:10:43.870
Accept me.

00:10:48.710 --> 00:10:52.290
I can't... I can't put myself out there.

00:10:54.040 --> 00:10:57.550
I hate that I'm like this.

00:10:59.880 --> 00:11:02.510
Did you get a reply?

00:11:02.510 --> 00:11:04.970
She said she has to practice for the play.

00:11:04.970 --> 00:11:07.100
That's too bad.

00:11:07.100 --> 00:11:12.350
Ugh, and I wanted to eat lunch with her.

00:11:13.270 --> 00:11:18.570
I never knew that Shizuko was so stubborn.

00:11:20.530 --> 00:11:24.370
I wonder what's going on with her.

00:11:24.370 --> 00:11:28.410
I'm sure this Shizuku-chan
is Shizuku-chan, too.

00:11:28.410 --> 00:11:29.830
Huh?

00:11:29.830 --> 00:11:33.710
I was sort of like that, so I understand.

00:11:33.710 --> 00:11:36.460
Not liking yourself.

00:11:38.550 --> 00:11:44.430
In my case, Ai-san pulled me away from that.

00:11:44.430 --> 00:11:47.810
And then all of you cheered me up.

00:11:47.810 --> 00:11:50.430
That's why... I was able to do my concert.

00:11:51.480 --> 00:11:54.270
I have Ai-san.

00:11:55.270 --> 00:11:57.020
And Shizuku-chan needs...

00:11:58.900 --> 00:12:01.280
I'm gonna go!

00:12:03.410 --> 00:12:04.620
Fight!

00:12:05.820 --> 00:12:08.870
I wish to wash my Irish wristwatch.

00:12:08.870 --> 00:12:11.370
Peter Piper picked a peck of pickled peppers.

00:12:11.370 --> 00:12:14.210
Can you can a can as a canner can can a can?

00:12:14.210 --> 00:12:17.250
How can a clam cram in a clean cream can?

00:12:17.250 --> 00:12:20.300
She sells seashells by the seashore.

00:12:20.300 --> 00:12:23.130
I saw Susie sitting in a shoeshine shop.

00:12:23.130 --> 00:12:25.720
Tom threw Tim three thumbtacks.

00:12:25.720 --> 00:12:27.260
I thought I thought of
thinking of thanking you...

00:12:28.970 --> 00:12:30.770
Found you.

00:12:30.770 --> 00:12:32.310
Kasumi-san?

00:12:36.900 --> 00:12:38.860
Wh-What brings you here?

00:12:38.860 --> 00:12:41.490
What brings me here? Well...

00:12:43.570 --> 00:12:47.320
We parted really awkwardly yesterday.

00:12:47.320 --> 00:12:51.080
So I wanted to see how you were doing.

00:12:52.370 --> 00:12:54.960
Sorry to make you worry.

00:12:54.960 --> 00:12:57.380
But I'm really okay.

00:12:57.380 --> 00:12:58.960
The audition will be--

00:13:00.590 --> 00:13:03.470
Stare...

00:13:05.380 --> 00:13:08.050
Your eyes are a little puffy.

00:13:10.100 --> 00:13:14.310
I totally get that you're
the stubborn type now.

00:13:15.640 --> 00:13:16.850
But...

00:13:19.860 --> 00:13:23.240
Don't try to frantically hide
while making that face!

00:13:23.240 --> 00:13:25.700
I thought we were friends!

00:13:32.080 --> 00:13:34.160
This role...

00:13:34.160 --> 00:13:37.750
I was told I need to put myself out there.

00:13:37.750 --> 00:13:40.960
But I can't do that.

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:44.920
I've always...

00:13:44.920 --> 00:13:50.350
...liked old movies and novels
ever since I was little.

00:13:50.350 --> 00:13:56.690
But I was the only kid like that...
so it made me anxious.

00:13:56.690 --> 00:13:59.690
Every time someone looked at me weird,

00:13:59.690 --> 00:14:02.150
I thought they were going to hate me.

00:14:03.480 --> 00:14:10.490
Eventually, I got scared of anyone
seeing me as different in any way.

00:14:10.490 --> 00:14:13.950
That's why I started acting.

00:14:13.950 --> 00:14:17.830
I wanted to act out the good girl
that everyone liked.

00:14:17.830 --> 00:14:22.380
Then... I felt a little better.

00:14:22.380 --> 00:14:24.130
Shizuko...

00:14:25.050 --> 00:14:30.550
I just can't put myself out there.

00:14:31.470 --> 00:14:35.850
If that's necessary to become
an actor a school idol...

00:14:36.640 --> 00:14:40.150
...that means I... can't be either!

00:14:42.690 --> 00:14:44.940
I can't express myself.

00:14:44.940 --> 00:14:48.610
I'm scared of... people hating me.

00:14:57.040 --> 00:14:59.040
How can you say...

00:15:00.040 --> 00:15:03.460
...something so naive?!

00:15:07.670 --> 00:15:10.380
Who cares if people might dislike you?

00:15:10.380 --> 00:15:14.050
Just look at how cute I am!

00:15:14.050 --> 00:15:16.810
Even then, there are some people
who won't compliment me!

00:15:16.810 --> 00:15:21.560
And you've never called me cute, either!

00:15:21.560 --> 00:15:23.650
So what do you think about me?

00:15:23.650 --> 00:15:26.530
Huh? I, uh...

00:15:26.530 --> 00:15:30.070
Am I cute? Am I not cute?!

00:15:30.070 --> 00:15:33.490
I-I think you're probably cute...

00:15:33.490 --> 00:15:36.450
See! You said it just fine!

00:15:36.450 --> 00:15:38.540
Now let's talk about you!

00:15:38.540 --> 00:15:42.250
The fact that you're surprisingly
stubborn and obstinate...

00:15:42.250 --> 00:15:45.920
And the fact that you're not actually
that confident... All of that!

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:47.920
None of those are compliments.

00:15:47.920 --> 00:15:53.590
There might be people
who say they don't like you...

00:15:53.590 --> 00:15:58.270
...but I love everything
about you, Shizuku Osaka!

00:15:59.890 --> 00:16:03.440
So you don't have to worry...

00:16:06.020 --> 00:16:07.520
I'm going home!

00:16:07.520 --> 00:16:09.610
Hey, wait.

00:16:09.610 --> 00:16:15.950
You made me say all that,
so you better win that second audition!

00:16:56.990 --> 00:17:03.120
Himeno. Apparently, the lead in this play
is a school idol at Nijigasaki.

00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:05.170
I see.

00:17:14.470 --> 00:17:15.680
Okay.

00:17:17.390 --> 00:17:20.850
I'm so happy that Shizuku-chan
passed the audition again.

00:17:20.850 --> 00:17:24.310
Now I'm starting to get nervous.

00:17:26.310 --> 00:17:28.860
It's starting.

00:17:28.860 --> 00:17:31.110
You've got this, Shizuko.

00:17:38.870 --> 00:17:41.990
In a certain theater in a certain city,

00:17:41.990 --> 00:17:44.500
there was a girl.

00:17:44.500 --> 00:17:48.710
Her dream was to become
the best singer in town.

00:17:48.710 --> 00:17:53.130
And to have as many people
hear her song as possible.

00:17:53.130 --> 00:17:56.880
I want to be your ideal heroine.

00:17:58.140 --> 00:18:03.020
Please wait! Why am I the only one
not allowed to perform?

00:18:03.020 --> 00:18:07.390
Sorry, but your songs aren't that popular.

00:18:07.390 --> 00:18:11.610
I won't be able to let you
stand on our stage anymore.

00:18:12.980 --> 00:18:18.820
Hey, wait! Let's ask the owner
to give you one more chance!

00:18:18.820 --> 00:18:20.660
It's over!

00:18:25.700 --> 00:18:27.620
Are you that scared...

00:18:29.250 --> 00:18:32.130
...to show your true self?

00:18:32.130 --> 00:18:33.420
Wait!

00:18:34.510 --> 00:18:36.720
Even then...

00:18:36.720 --> 00:18:39.050
...I want to sing.

00:18:50.270 --> 00:18:52.980
I'd been ignoring you this whole time.

00:18:54.230 --> 00:19:00.030
But I want to sing.
I'm sure that feeling is real.

00:19:00.030 --> 00:19:02.490
I'm sorry about everything.

00:19:06.950 --> 00:19:12.170
This is me. The true me
that I cannot escape from.

00:19:12.170 --> 00:19:14.460
People may hate you.

00:19:14.460 --> 00:19:18.050
But there were people who said they loved me.

00:19:18.050 --> 00:19:23.430
Then... I'll just have to
start over again on this small stage.

00:19:39.280 --> 00:19:41.780
The thunder echoes in my heart

00:19:41.780 --> 00:19:45.530
And all of the emotions I've
kept trapped inside start to spill out

00:19:45.530 --> 00:19:48.250
I'll never lose sight

00:19:48.250 --> 00:19:50.290
Of my own feelings again

00:19:50.290 --> 00:19:56.090
The raindrops that fall down from the sky

00:19:56.090 --> 00:20:02.300
Drip, drip down my cheeks

00:20:02.300 --> 00:20:05.010
And before I knew it

00:20:05.010 --> 00:20:08.600
It gently washes away

00:20:08.600 --> 00:20:15.060
The mask that was covering my heart

00:20:15.060 --> 00:20:21.150
There was something in my heart

00:20:21.150 --> 00:20:23.780
That refused to change

00:20:23.780 --> 00:20:27.530
And I finally realized it

00:20:27.530 --> 00:20:30.870
I powerfully awaken

00:20:30.870 --> 00:20:34.040
Let's go run barefoot

00:20:34.040 --> 00:20:39.960
I won't run away from myself anymore

00:20:39.960 --> 00:20:43.050
When I'm able to accept and embrace

00:20:43.050 --> 00:20:46.470
All of my worries and fears

00:20:46.470 --> 00:20:53.600
I'll be able to journey
into that blindingly bright sky

00:21:30.430 --> 00:21:32.310
That was fantastic!

00:21:32.310 --> 00:21:35.230
This was truly a performance that only
the school idol Shizuku Osaka-san

00:21:35.230 --> 00:21:37.690
could have pulled off!

00:21:37.690 --> 00:21:39.060
Thank you very much!

00:21:39.060 --> 00:21:44.990
Do you have a message for our readers
as an actor and a school idol?

00:21:44.990 --> 00:21:48.530
Please see me for who I am.

00:22:05.800 --> 00:22:08.590
<i>As we slowly run down this path</i>

00:22:08.590 --> 00:22:12.470
<i>Something is trying to come to life</i>

00:22:12.470 --> 00:22:19.310
<i>I want to tell you, I want to tell you that</i>

00:22:19.310 --> 00:22:22.110
<i>The sky that we look up at every day</i>

00:22:22.110 --> 00:22:26.070
<i>Has a blue that changes with the seasons</i>

00:22:26.070 --> 00:22:32.700
<i>There are no rules, it's telling us</i>
<i>to depict it however we please</i>

00:22:32.700 --> 00:22:35.000
<i>Let's not be in a hurry!</i>

00:22:35.000 --> 00:22:39.460
<i>Let's enjoy this thrilling time even more!</i>

00:22:39.460 --> 00:22:47.550
<i>Let's all pursue the things that we love</i>

00:22:48.470 --> 00:22:51.930
<i>We don't know where we're headed to just yet</i>

00:22:51.930 --> 00:22:55.020
<i>Hopefully, there's an exciting</i>
<i>future awaiting us</i>

00:22:55.020 --> 00:22:59.520
<i>It'd make me happy</i>
<i>if we can both smile about that</i>

00:22:59.520 --> 00:23:02.150
<i>Thank you again today</i>

00:23:02.150 --> 00:23:05.400
<i>Now, let us open up our very own maps</i>

00:23:05.400 --> 00:23:08.570
<i>And casually take flight</i>

00:23:08.570 --> 00:23:13.870
<i>I want to dream, aspire, and dream once again</i>

00:23:13.870 --> 00:23:18.080
<i>I just want to keep dreaming!</i>

00:23:22.750 --> 00:23:24.460
That was a lovely performance.

00:23:24.460 --> 00:23:25.550
Yes.

00:23:27.300 --> 00:23:31.840
The Nijigasaki High School Idol Club...

00:23:31.840 --> 00:23:34.140
How interesting.

00:23:36.390 --> 00:23:39.310
Next time, "Friends but Rivals."
